{"term":"franchise","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:dcec10c3aa99949a1a","definition":"The right to vote at a public election or referendum; see: suffrage.","example":"","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"countable, uncountable","wordFamily":["disfranchise","effranchise","franchisal","franchisee","franchise fatigue","franchise player","franchiser","franchise records","franchisor","microfranchise","nonfranchise","subfranchise"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/franchise#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:d80bae5616e7fe5159","definition":"A right or privilege officially granted to a person, a group of people, or a company by a government.","example":"a. 1872, William H. Seward, debate\nElection by universal suffrage, as modified by the Constitution, is the one crowning franchise of the American people.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"countable, uncountable","wordFamily":["disfranchise","effranchise","franchisal","franchisee","franchise fatigue","franchise player","franchiser","franchise records","franchisor","microfranchise","nonfranchise","subfranchise"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/franchise#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:8fa6b0283e2e5f4980","definition":"An acknowledgment of a corporation's existence and ownership.","example":"","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"countable, uncountable","wordFamily":["disfranchise","effranchise","franchisal","franchisee","franchise fatigue","franchise player","franchiser","franchise records","franchisor","microfranchise","nonfranchise","subfranchise"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"htt