aikki:684e4266016401e36a","definition":"The membership of a corporation or state; citizenship.","example":"","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"countable, uncountable","wordFamily":["disfranchise","effranchise","franchisal","franchisee","franchise fatigue","franchise player","franchiser","franchise records","franchisor","microfranchise","nonfranchise","subfranchise"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/franchise#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:b1f1651763cf76c4db","definition":"The district or jurisdiction to which a particular privilege extends; the limits of an immunity; hence, an asylum or sanctuary.","example":"Churches and monasteries in Spain are franchises for criminals.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"countable, uncountable","wordFamily":["disfranchise","effranchise","franchisal","franchisee","franchise fatigue","franchise player","franchiser","franchise records","franchisor","microfranchise","nonfranchise","subfranchise"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/franchise#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:5c04da6d0bad2cf358","definition":"The collection of organizations in the history of a sports team; the tradition of a sports team as an entity, extending beyond the contemporary organization.","example":"The Whalers' home city of Hartford was one of many for the franchise.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"countable, uncountable","wordFamily":["disfranchise","effranchise","franchisal","franchisee","franchise fatigue","franchise player","franchiser","franchise records","franchisor","microfranchise","nonfranchise","subfranchise"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/franchise#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:c26435d59102f21bd5","definition":"The positive influence on the buying behavior of customers exerted by the reputation of a company or a brand.","example":"Once a brand has established a consumer franchise and a brand image, it takes a long time for these to decay, as the image is maintained more by people's personal familiarity with and usage of the brand than by external marketing stimuli.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"countable, uncountable","wordFamily":["disfranchise","effranchise","franchisal","franchisee","franchise fatigue","franchise player","franchiser","franchise records","franchisor","microfranchise","nonfranchise","subfranchise"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/franchise#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:a830e795debd70e335","definition":"The loose collection of fictional works pertaining to a particular fictional universe, including literary, film, or television series from various sources, generally when all authorized by a copyright holder or similar authority.","example":"the Star Wars franchise","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"countable, uncountable","wordFamily":["disfranchise","effranchise","franchisal","franchisee","franchise fatigue","franchise player","franchiser","franchise records","franchisor","microfranchise","nonfranchise","subfranchise"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/franchise#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:6176e8b8a097af72bc","definition":"Exemption from constraint or oppression; freedom; liberty.","example":"Ye[…]the love of ladies foule defame;\nTo whom the world this franchise ever yeelded,\nThat of their loves choise they might freedom clame.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"countable, uncountable","wordFamily":["disfranchise","effranchise","franchisal","franchisee","franchise fatigue","franchise player","franchiser","franchise records","franchisor","microfranchise","nonfranchise","subfranchise"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/franchise#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:560519f4ae71899f20","definition":"Magnanimity; generosity; liberality; frankness; nobility.","example":"","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"obsolete","register":"countable, obsolete, uncountable","wordFamily":["disfranchise","effranchise","franchisal","franchisee","franchise fatigue","franchise player","franchiser","franchise records","franchisor","microfranchise","nonfranchise","subfranchise"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/franchise#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:4833cda9c20eac4b08","definition":"To confer certain powers on; grant a franchise to; authorize.","example":"In a Commons Written Reply to Shadow Rail Minister Tan Dhesi, regarding any assessment of the impact on open access operators by the decision to move away from franchising […], Heaton-Harris highlighted that non-franchised operators run trains without a contractual relationship with Government.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["disfranchise","effranchise","franchisal","franchisee","franchise fatigue","franchise player","franchiser","franchise records","franchisor","microfranchise","nonfranchise","subfranchise","franchisability","franchisable"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","at